            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A semiconductor laser device comprising: semiconductor laser elements (170); a substrate (100) having a heat dissipation portion (101), an insulating portion (102), and a metal film (103); a cover (120); and a base member (110). The heat dissipation portion and the metal film are not electrically connected. The base member includes a bottom part (118) having an arrangement surface on which the semiconductor laser elements are arranged, a lateral surface (119), and a bottom surface that is bonded to the heat dissipation portion; and a frame part (111) having an upper surface to which the cover is bonded, and a bottom surface that is bonded to the metal film. The bottom part and the frame part contain a metal and a ceramic, respectively, as a main material, or the bottom part has a higher thermal conductivity than the frame part. The arrangement surface of the bottom part has a rectangular shape. The frame part has a bonding surface (113) to which the bottom part is bonded, a first inner lateral surface (115) that intersects with the bonding surface and forms a frame larger than the arrangement surface, a second inner lateral surface (116) that intersects with the bonding surface and forms a frame smaller than the arrangement surface, a planar surface that is located opposite to the bonding surface and intersects a portion of the second inner lateral surface, a first electrode layer (112) that is provided on the bottom surface of the frame part, and a second electrode layer (114) that is provided on the planar surface. The first electrode layer is electrically connected to the metal film. The semiconductor laser elements are arranged in a closed space.</p>
            </abstract>
